 "narrative": {
  "northStar": "Graphite and ink",
  "overview": "A quiet graphite page with one dark accent, so the only colour on screen is the day itself. Every kind of time keeps its own ink, and it is the ink, not the frame, that tells you what an hour was for. Fine one-pixel lines, no ornament, no glow. Layout, navigation and controls stay the standard ones for a phone app.",
  "keyCharacteristics": [
   "One accent band: bottom bar on phones, side rail from 960px; near black in light, near white in dark.",
   "Category inks on a 9% tint of themselves for each block row.",
   "Hour amounts set as large Spectral denomination numerals at the end of each row.",
   "The guilloche rosette as ميزان اليوم and ميزان الأسبوع, and as the app icon: on the graphite accent `#1F1F22`, one half navy `#9EBDFA` and one half amber `#D9884B`, ring `#ECECEA` (feature 033).",
   "Fine one-pixel line work only; no ornament, no glow."
  ],
  "rules": [
   {
    "name": "The Denomination Rule",
    "body": "A category's ink is its identity everywhere: row tint, check circle, denomination numeral, week strip segment and rosette petals. Never use a category ink for anything that is not that category.",
    "section": "colors"
   },
   {
    "name": "The Two Halves Rule",
    "body": "University and course form one half of the balance, work and life the other. A kind the user adds joins one half, or neither when it is not about either (its own choice in the editor).",
    "section": "colors"
   },
   {
    "name": "The Isolated Number Rule",
    "body": "Hour amounts with fractions (1½, 8¼) are wrapped in LTR isolates so they never reorder inside Arabic text.",
    "section": "typography"
   }
  ],
  "dos": [
   "Do keep every category ink at AA on paper, on cards, on its own tint and on the grained paper.",
   "Do mark a state with a shape or a word as well as a colour, as the late icon does.",
   "Do show amounts of time as denominations, not as progress rings.",
   "Do keep line work at one pixel.",
   "Do keep the paper grain on the ground only, faint enough that every ink holds AA."
  ],
  "donts": [
   "Don't add Islamic ornament, mosque or Mushaf motifs.",
   "Don't use neon, glow or gradients.",
   "Don't colour the frame or add a second palette: the kinds' inks are the only colour.",
   "Don't use a category ink for decoration.",
   "Don't put the grain on cards, or turn it into a pattern or a motif."
  ]
 }
}
